{
  format: 1
  name: string-search-does-not-normalize-unicode
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#expressions", "§6.5", "#annex-a", "§A.1"]
  tags: ["unicode"]
  note: '''
    Attack: feed the search predicates canonically-equivalent but differently
    encoded text — an NFC needle (c, a, f, U+00E9) against an NFD subject
    (c, a, f, e, U+0301, s) — hoping the engine normalizes and reports a match
    the stored scalars do not support (or, in the other direction, hoping a
    normalizing engine reports a match a prefix-sensitive accounting rule would
    then trust).

    §6.5 pins the answer: comparison is over Unicode scalar values, with no
    normalization, so a predicate holds exactly when the needle's scalar
    sequence decomposes the subject's. Annex A.1: a `text` value is a Unicode
    scalar sequence, preserved exactly. Writing the two encodings as

      nfd = c a f e U+0301 s        nfc = c a f U+00E9 s
      nfd_needle = c a f e U+0301   nfc_needle = c a f U+00E9

    the six expectations follow from the scalar sequences alone:

      starts_with(nfd, nfc_needle) = false — nfd's 4th scalar is e, not U+00E9
      starts_with(nfc, nfc_needle) = true
      starts_with(nfd, nfd_needle) = true  — nfd matches its own encoding
      starts_with(nfc, nfd_needle) = false
      contains(nfd, U+0301)        = true  — the combining acute is a scalar of nfd
      contains(nfc, U+0301)        = false — nfc carries no combining acute

    Every Unicode value below is written with explicit \uXXXX escapes so no
    editor or tool can silently renormalize the case file.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.strnfc@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      words: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        word: "text"
        nfc_prefix: "= string.starts_with(.word, 'caf\u00e9')"
        nfd_prefix: "= string.starts_with(.word, 'cafe\u0301')"
        has_combining: "= string.contains(.word, '\u0301')"
      }
      $public: {
        words: { $view: ".words { id, nfc_prefix, nfd_prefix, has_combining, $sort: [id] }" }
      }
    }
    $data: {
      words: {
        nfc: { word: "caf\u00e9s" }
        nfd: { word: "cafe\u0301s" }
      }
    }
  }

  steps: [
    { watch: "public.words", id: "w1",
      expect_init: { value: [
        { id: "nfc", nfc_prefix: true, nfd_prefix: false, has_combining: false }
        { id: "nfd", nfc_prefix: false, nfd_prefix: true, has_combining: true }
      ] } }
  ]
}
